0..77 Comment "// Loop-carried state. A `while` or a `loop` that names a slot held around it"
78..152 Comment "// carries the slot through its passes: each pass reads the value the pass"
153..230 Comment "// before left there, and what follows the loop reads the value the last pass"
231..309 Comment "// left. The loop is a fold whose accumulator is the slot (Hutton, \"A tutorial"
310..384 Comment "// on the universality and expressiveness of fold\", _Journal of Functional"
385..461 Comment "// Programming_ 9(4), 1999). A loop may run forever, so each function states"
462..494 Comment "// `Partial` in its row (#1481)."
496..571 Comment "/// A count held at three and taken down by one on each pass: the condition"
572..646 Comment "/// reads the value the pass before wrote back, so the loop stops at zero."
